        ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & -4 \\\\ 5 & k & 3 \\\\ -8 & -4 & -6\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -4 & -6\\end{aligned}|)+((4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -8 & -6\\end{aligned}|)+((-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -8 & -4\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (-6)-(3)\\cdot (-4)))+((4)\\cdot ((5)\\cdot (-6)-(3)\\cdot (-8)))+((-4)\\cdot ((5)\\cdot (-4)-(k)\\cdot (-8)))\\\\ &=((-2)\\cdot (12-6k))+((4)\\cdot (-6))+((-4)\\cdot (8k-20))\\\\ &=(12k-24)+(-24)+(80-32k)\\\\ &=32-20k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}32-20k&=0\\\\ -20k&=-32\\\\ k&=\\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{8}{5}.$",
